@page
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Body Recomposition Evidence | 12 Week Recomp";
    ViewData["Description"] = "See the evidence base behind 12 Week Recomp: resistance training, nutrition, fat loss, lean mass, and individualized application.";
    ViewData["CanonicalPath"] = "/evidence";
}

<section class="section hero" style="padding-top:58px">
  <div class="shell evidence-hero-grid">
    <div>
      <span class="kicker">Evidence</span>
      <h1>Coaching explains the output of the individualized physiology model.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        12 Week Recomp turns established body-recomposition principles into an individualized
        recommendation engine, daily coach messages, and weekly progress guidance.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-card evidence-hero-photo">
      <img src="/assets/coach-training.jpg" alt="Cassie, Marisol, and Steve coaching resistance training">
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section alt">
  <div class="shell grid-2">
    <article class="study">
      <div class="tag">10-week study • 2026</div>
      <h3>Resistance-trained participants</h3>
      <div class="metric-pairs">
        <div class="metric"><strong>−6.5 lb</strong><span>fat mass</span></div>
        <div class="metric"><strong>+2.3 lb</strong><span>fat-free mass</span></div>
      </div>
      <p>
        Approximate group-average change from the cited resistance-trained sample.
        The practical point: losing fat while gaining or preserving lean mass is a real target.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="study">
      <div class="tag">4-week controlled trial • 2016</div>
      <h3>High protein + aggressive deficit + intense training</h3>
      <div class="metric-pairs">
        <div class="metric"><strong>−10.6 lb</strong><span>fat mass</span></div>
        <div class="metric"><strong>+2.6 lb</strong><span>lean mass</span></div>
      </div>
      <p>
        A strong illustration that fat loss and lean-mass improvement can occur together
        when training, protein, energy intake, and recovery are aligned.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="callout">
      <h3>Evidence alone is not enough. Translation matters.</h3>
      <p>
        12 Week Recomp translates the science into an individualized recommendation engine,
        coach-style daily messaging, and weekly progress feedback that helps users apply the
        principles consistently.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section alt">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2>The principles have to work in the real world.</h2>
      <p>
        Training quality and nutrition quality are not competing ideas. The program is built
        around matching the food to the work while protecting the muscle-building signal.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="evidence-photo-grid">
      <article class="photo-card evidence-photo-card">
        <img src="/assets/coach-training.jpg" alt="Cassie, Marisol, and Steve working through strength-training technique">
        <div class="photo-copy">
          <div class="eyebrow">Resistance training</div>
          <h3>Create a reason for the body to keep or build muscle.</h3>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="photo-card evidence-photo-card">
        <img src="/assets/coach-mealprep-2.jpg" alt="Cassie, Marisol, and Steve preparing practical meals together">
        <div class="photo-copy">
          <div class="eyebrow">Nutrition + consistency</div>
          <h3>Support the work with food you can actually repeat.</h3>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="shell split">
    <div class="panel">
      <img src="/assets/body-recovery.png" alt="12 Week Recomp body and recovery screen">
    </div>
    <div class="panel">
      <img src="/assets/training-entry.png" alt="12 Week Recomp training entry screen">
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2>What users experience</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="grid-3">
      <article class="feature-card">
        <div class="icon">A</div>
        <h3>Daily recommendations</h3>
        <p>
          Not just “eat less” or “work harder.” Users get structured guidance shaped by
          the day’s demand and recovery context.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <div class="icon">B</div>
        <h3>Daily coach tone</h3>
        <p>
          The same physiological recommendation can be delivered through different coach
          personalities, making the platform feel more human and useful.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <div class="icon">C</div>
        <h3>Weekly review loop</h3>
        <p>
          Weekly notifications and hints keep the user learning: what improved,
          what to watch, and how to make the next week better.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section alt">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="callout">
      <h3>$20 for 12 weeks — built to teach, not trap.</h3>
      <p>
        The goal is capability: learn the principles, build habits, understand your own
        training and nutrition patterns, and carry that knowledge forward instead of depending
        on a forever subscription.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
